{
  "case_id": "2009-08-876",
  "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For two decades, courts of appeals confronting Section 1346 have been unanimous on, at most, three points.\nThe first one is that the unvarnished text of the statute is vague, amorphous, open-ended, and essentially, not very helpful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 08-876, Conrad Black et al. v. The United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You -- you don't ask for the first, do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Are -- are you saying that unless we adopt the limiting instruction that you propose, the statute is then vague?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that is not a fair statement, Mr. Chief Justice. I think the D.C. Circuit's opinion, of course, is indeed very helpful, but it was a -- a distillation of what other courts of appeals have told the government again and again, in Ballard in the Fifth Circuit, in Feldman in the Seventh, in --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "event, we fully support -- actually, we support anyway -- the -- the brief that was filed by the Chamber of Commerce and the National Association of Criminal Defense Lawyers, for the proposition that as an essential matter, this statute cannot be saved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT THAT WOULD FIT YOUR TEST, THOUGH."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THE COURTS OF APPEALS HAVE -- HAVE RULED THAT AN INTENT TO INTERFERE WITH THE PROPERTY RIGHTS OF THE GOVERNMENT WAS NOT AN ELEMENT OF THE CORE MEANING OF THE FRAUD."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THE PETITIONER TODAY HAS SOUGHT TO PRESENT A QUESTION TO THIS COURT THAT HE CHOSE NOT TO INCLUDE IN HIS QUESTIONS PRESENTED, WHETHER THE STATUTE IS UNCONSTITUTIONALLY VAGUE IN ALL OF ITS APPLICATIONS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHAT THIS STATUTE IS, JUSTICE KENNEDY, IS CONGRESS'S EFFORT TO REINSTATE THE BODY OF LAW THAT THIS COURT HELD WAS NOT A VALID CONSTRUCTION OF THE MAIL FRAUD STATUTE."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me, may I ask you to put -- in terms of your brief, you said your definition of materiality -- you said materiality is related to but different from what Mr. Estrada is urging the Court to adopt: economic harm to the victim. So can you tell us how materiality is related to economic harm to the victim and how it is different from economic harm to the victim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben (Government)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is related to it, Justice Ginsburg, in that in a business setting materiality will be in most cases coextensive with economic harm at least if economic harm is conceived as I conceive it, and as the cases have conceived of it as extending to things like harm to reputation that will interfere with a business's ability to go forward."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That -- that is Altshuler B, which I -- that seems to work, but then you want to go beyond that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just a few points, Mr. Chief Justice. First, it bear emphasis that the government has once again said that this is a federal obligation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-876",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bf2987868f882d2ee84397a8b2e4d7d0a10d76382c6f9e0f7efd0107bd37e776",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf2987868f88-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:18 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
